# Local configuration. `*.local` below covers Vite's .env.local and friends; these are
# the ones it does not. The Firebase web config is public by design, but a file called
# .env is where a real secret ends up sooner or later.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Credentials.
#
# The one mistake here that cannot be walked back. A Firebase service account
# key is full admin on the project: it bypasses `firestore.rules` entirely, so
# it reads every child's name and every parent's phone number regardless of
# what the rules say. The console hands them out as a download, which lands in
# whatever directory the browser is pointed at — often this one.
#
# Named widely on purpose. Nothing in this app needs one: it is a browser app
# with no server, and the emulator scripts use the emulator's own fake owner
# token.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*serviceAccount*.json
*-adminsdk-*.json
*firebase-adminsdk*
*.pem
*.p12
*.key

# Dependencies / build
node_modules/
dist/
coverage/
test-results/
*.local
*.tsbuildinfo

# Firebase
.firebase/
.runtimeconfig.json

# Logs, all of them. None belongs in here, and the ones worth having are named
# by whatever produced them — a blanket rule is fewer things to remember than a
# list that has to grow every time a tool is added.
*.log

# Local process bookkeeping from `make up` and `make firstrun`.
*.pid

# Emulator snapshots (regenerate from scripts; never commit real data)
seed/
firebase-export-*/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PII — the Apple Day workbook and every export derived from it contain youth
# names, parent names, emails and phone numbers. None of it belongs in git.
# Keep the source workbook and any generated person data local only.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.xlsx
*.xls
data/local/
*.responses.csv

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One group's own setup, which is not this app.
#
# A shop list is real businesses, their pitches and their group codes — useful to
# whoever wrote it and to nobody else. Committing one would hand every other group
# a location library it has to empty before it can start.
#
# Write your own if you want the emulator pre-filled; `make seed` says what shape
# it takes, and `make firstrun` needs none of it.
data/locations.seed.json

# Which Firebase projects to deploy to, and under what alias. Real project ids
# for real groups; `.firebaserc.example` shows the shape. Same reasoning as
# `.env` above — this is configuration for one installation, not the app.
.firebaserc

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

